# Recordings. Kept on disk deliberately - CALIBRATION.md treats them as journal
# evidence and --replay runs against them - but they are tens of megabytes of
# binary that git can only store whole, and a new one is produced every session.
*.wav

# Listener output and analysis runs. Regenerated on every start; snap.log is
# held open by the running listener.
*.log
*.log.session*
*.marker

# Superseded by version control itself.
*.bak-*
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Calibration output. The journals record one person's room, microphone and
# voice levels, and the recording they were derived from is a *.wav that this
# file already excludes - so a journal on its own cannot be re-derived or
# checked by anyone else. Kept on disk, where --derive can still reach them.
calibration/*.json

# Config snapshots and hand-tuning leftovers from the sessions that produced
# the shipped defaults. Real provenance, but local: nothing in the code or the
# documentation reads them.
snapshots/
orig-working.json
